From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ftrace: Remove a freed range's records with one memmove

ftrace_free_mem() takes the records in the freed range out of their
page one at a time: a bsearch() for the next one, then a memmove() of
everything after it in the page. Freeing init memory removes the record
of every traced __init function, 1,989 on this kernel, and they sit
together in the last page group, so its tail is moved once for each.

The records in a page are sorted, so those in a range are contiguous:
find the first and the last around the one bsearch() returns, and take
them all out with one memmove(). What each record is handed to - the
list of hash entries to clear, the module map - is unchanged.

Checked on this kernel with a walk of every record after
ftrace_free_init_mem() (an experiment build, not part of this patch):
40,118 records left, none in init memory, none out of order, and
ftrace_free_mem() took 59 us.

Measured in a KVM guest on a laptop, not nested (QEMU q35, two vCPUs,
10 boots each, interleaved; a lead, not the bench fleet): the time from
"VFS: Pivoted into new rootfs" to "Freeing unused kernel image" 2.7 ms
p50 before, and under 1.1 ms after, below what the probe lists. On the
bench fleet the gap was 2.6 ms nested and on bare metal alike (lab runs
44563496308, 44563512999).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/trace/ftrace.c | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/trace/ftrace.c b/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
index 250ccce13..e7ae108a7 100644
--- a/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
@@ -8392,24 +8392,43 @@ void ftrace_free_mem(struct module *mod, void *start_ptr, void *end_ptr)
 		mod_map = allocate_ftrace_mod_map(mod, start, end);
 
 	for (pg = ftrace_pages_start; pg; last_pg = &pg->next, pg = *last_pg) {
+		struct dyn_ftrace *first, *stop;
+		unsigned long index = pg->index;
+
 		if (end < pg->records[0].ip ||
 		    start >= (pg->records[pg->index - 1].ip + MCOUNT_INSN_SIZE))
 			continue;
- again:
+
 		rec = bsearch(&key, pg->records, pg->index,
 			      sizeof(struct dyn_ftrace),
 			      ftrace_cmp_recs);
 		if (!rec)
 			continue;
 
-		/* rec will be cleared from hashes after ftrace_lock unlock */
-		add_to_clear_hash_list(&clear_hash, rec);
-
-		if (mod_map)
-			save_ftrace_mod_rec(mod_map, rec);
+		/*
+		 * The records are sorted, so those in the range are the ones
+		 * either side of the one found. Take them out with a single
+		 * memmove(), not one each: freeing init memory moved the rest
+		 * of the page once for every __init function in it.
+		 */
+		first = rec;
+		while (first > pg->records &&
+		       (first - 1)->ip + MCOUNT_INSN_SIZE > start)
+			first--;
+		stop = rec + 1;
+		while (stop < pg->records + index && stop->ip <= end)
+			stop++;
+
+		for (rec = first; rec < stop; rec++) {
+			/* rec will be cleared from hashes after ftrace_lock unlock */
+			add_to_clear_hash_list(&clear_hash, rec);
+
+			if (mod_map)
+				save_ftrace_mod_rec(mod_map, rec);
+		}
 
-		pg->index--;
-		ftrace_update_tot_cnt--;
+		pg->index -= stop - first;
+		ftrace_update_tot_cnt -= stop - first;
 		if (!pg->index) {
 			*last_pg = pg->next;
 			pg->next = tmp_page;
@@ -8419,10 +8438,8 @@ void ftrace_free_mem(struct module *mod, void *start_ptr, void *end_ptr)
 				ftrace_pages = pg;
 			continue;
 		}
-		memmove(rec, rec + 1,
-			(pg->index - (rec - pg->records)) * sizeof(*rec));
-		/* More than one function may be in this block */
-		goto again;
+		memmove(first, stop,
+			(pg->records + index - stop) * sizeof(*rec));
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&ftrace_lock);
 
-- 
